# v0.28.0 — post-reset tasks (staging)

**Tag**: `v0.28.0` (pending).


### ISLAND-FOLLOWUP-1

- `IslandHubSilent` summary corrected to "25+ minutes": the 600 s gauge
  boundary plus `for: 15m` makes the earliest fire ~25 minutes, not the
  15 the old text implied. `IslandGossipSilent` renamed to
  `IslandImportSilent` and reworded to "No block import": the feed runs
  on every accepted import (gossip, subscription sync, pull), verified
  live 25 Oct — node0 imported 997 blocks via subscription and 0 via
  gossip in 24 h with no false alert. Gauge names unchanged
  (`aitbc_island_gossip_silence_seconds` still measures import silence);
  expressions, thresholds and `for:` values unchanged. promtool
  check + test green on node2 (island section; two BridgeSet failures
  pre-exist on main).

### PLAY3 MCP option forwarding

- Generated CLI-mirroring MCP tools now carry options declared on a
  command's top-level Click group (e.g. `aitbc wallet --wallet-name
  --wallet-path --use-daemon --chain-id`, `aitbc market --wallet
  --wallet-path --password-file`, `aitbc coin-requests --db`). They were
  previously dropped from the tool schema and the emitted argv, so an
  MCP-executed `wallet send` would silently use the ACTIVE wallet
  (SCENARIO-PLAY-3 SM-class `option-missing` on node0). Group options are
  emitted via `group_options` ahead of the subcommand tokens, matching
  Click parsing; leaf-redeclared flags keep their leaf position.
  Secret-value options (`--password`, `--password-stdin`) stay excluded
  per SM-03; `--password-file` is forwarded as a path. Refs #438.


### ISLAND-GAUGE-RENAME-1

- `aitbc_island_gossip_silence_seconds` counted every accepted import,
  not gossip — the name lied. The node now exports
  `aitbc_island_import_silence_seconds` bound to the same feed, and keeps
  the old name exported as a deprecated alias for one release. Alert
  rules (`IslandImportSilent`, `IslandHubSilent`) read the new name.
